: {"x": 1443.4, "y": 781.6, "width": 40.799999999999955, "height": 20.399999999999977}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Data presented as mean ‡ standard deviation. Statistically significant differences were determined by two-way ANOVA followed by Bonferroni's post hoc test, considering p < 0.05. Differences between control (C) and high-fat (HF) groups in the post hoc test are presented as *p < 0.05. n=5-7 samples per group. PYY, Peptide YY; GLP-1, Glucagon-like peptide-1, MD, Maternal diet, S, Offspring sex.", "bbox": {"x": 135.8, "y": 820.4, "width": 1382.4, "height": 73.60000000000002}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Maternal HF diet differently altered the dopamine signaling in the NAc depending on offspring sex, since there was an interaction effect (p<0.05) in the content of dopamine receptors (D1R and D2R), dopamine transporter (DAT) and cAMP-regulated neuronal phosphoprotein-32 kDa (DARPP-32) (Figures 7B-E, respectively). In these parameters, the male HF offspring presented a profile of increase while female HF offspring presented profile of decrease. There was a sex effect on the tyrosine hydroxylase (TH) content, a limiting enzyme of the dopamine synthesis, with female offspring presenting increased content (Sex effect, p<0.01), regardless of maternal diet (Figure 7A). Similarly, female HF offspring have increased DAT content (+ 82.5%, p<0.05) compared to male offspring, regardless of maternal diet (Figure 7D). Maternal HF diet decreased DARPP32 content in male offspring (- 46.3%, p<0.05) while increased in female offspring (+ 71.2%, p<0.05) (Figure 7E).", "bbox": {"x": 135.7, "y": 934.5, "width": 682.9000000000001, "height": 513.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "3.5 Food preference test", "bbox": {"x": 842.3, "y": 934.5, "width": 383.79999999999995, "height": 34.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Maternal HF diet induced higher preference for HF diet (+ 2.4-fold, p<0.05) in adolescent male offspring, while did not change the preference for C or HS diets (Figure 8). In the female offspring, maternal HF diet did not alter food preference in the adolescence (Figure 8) Representative blots are show in Figure 6E, F.", "bbox": {"x": 842.3, "y": 1002.0, "width": 675.9000000000001, "height": 204.4000000000001}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "4 Discussion", "bbox": {"x": 842.3, "y": 1284.5, "width": 220.79999999999995, "height": 30.59999999999991}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "In the present study, we characterized the presence of lipid endocannabinoids in breast milk of lactating rats and how maternal HF diet changes the levels of milk AEA and 2-AG in different time", "bbox": {"x": 845.5, "y": 1352.5, "width": 672.7, "height": 101.59999999999991}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "B", "bbox": {"x": 825.3, "y": 1556.4, "width": 27.200000000000045, "height": 17.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "2000•", "bbox": {"x": 869.5, "y": 1576.8, "width": 54.299999999999955, "height": 20.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "p=0.10", "bbox": {"x": 981.5, "y": 1570.0, "width": 54.299999999999955, "height": 20.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Milk AEA (ng/mL)", "bbox": {"x": 397.4, "y": 1624.4, "width": 23.80000000000001, "height": 159.70000000000005}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "2.0", "bbox": {"x": 434.7, "y": 1627.8, "width": 27.19999999999999, "height": 17.200000000000045}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.5", "bbox": {"x": 431.3, "y": 1773.9, "width": 34.0, "height": 17.09999999999991}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Milk 2-AG (ng/mL)", "bbox": {"x": 845.7, "y": 1621.0, "width": 20.399999999999977, "height": 166.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "1500-", "bbox": {"x": 869.5, "y": 1638.0, "width": 64.5, "height": 20.40000000000009}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "1000-", "bbox": {"x": 869.5, "y": 1699.0, "width": 64.5, "height": 21.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "500-", "bbox": {"x": 883.0, "y": 1760.0, "width": 50.89999999999998, "height": 17.299999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "P=0.054", "bbox": {"x": 1154.7, "y": 1631.0, "width": 74.70000000000005, "height": 27.299999999999955}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "0.0-", "bbox": {"x": 431.3, "y": 1821.0, "width": 37.39999999999998, "height": 17.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "11th day of Lactation", "bbox": {"x": 502.6, "y": 1835.8, "width": 105.39999999999998, "height": 43.80000000000018}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "21th day of Lactation", "bbox": {"x": 682.4, "y": 1845.0, "width": 102.39999999999998, "height": 35.5}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "11th day of Lactation", "bbox": {"x": 957.8, "y": 1841.9, "width": 105.29999999999995, "height": 41.09999999999991}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "21th day of Lactation", "bbox": {"x": 1137.7, "y": 1841.9, "width": 105.40000000000009, "height": 41.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "- C progenitor", "bbox": {"x": 675.2, "y": 1935.3, "width": 174.39999999999998, "height": 32.09999999999991}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "- HF progenitor", "bbox": {"x": 875.6, "y": 1934.7, "width": 184.60000000000002, "height": 33.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "FIGURE 4 Effect of high-fat (HF) diet on the content of endocannabinoids in the milk of rat progenitors. (A) Milk anandamide (AEA) and (B) 2-arachidonoylglycerol (2-AG) in the postnatal days 11 and 21 of control (C) and HF progenitors. Data are presented as mean + standard deviation and statistically significant differences were determined by unpaired Student's t test. *p < 0.05.", "bbox": {"x": 166.4, "y": 1994.6, "width": 1304.2, "height": 98.70000000000027}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Frontiers in Endocrinology", "bbox": {"x": 135.6, "y": 2220.5, "width": 245.00000000000003, "height": 26.300000000000182}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "08", "bbox": {"x": 808.3, "y": 2222.5, "width": 34.0, "height": 23.800000000000182}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "frontiersin.org", "bbox": {"x": 1385.3, "y": 2223.8, "width": 133.0, "height": 21.09999999999991}}], "ms": 279.57}